{"folioDeck": 1, "exportedAt": "2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z", "meta": {"id": "arabc", "title": "Arabic Alphabet", "subtitle": "31 letters and signs · both directions, as two cards per letter", "desc": "The 28 letters of the Arabic alphabet in their standard order, followed by the three spellings every first text uses — hamza (ء), tāʔ marbūṭa (ة) and alif maqṣūra (ى) — the first deck of the Arabic collection. Both directions: see a letter and recall its name and sound, or see its name and sound and recall the letter, each a card with its own schedule. Arabic is written right to left, and a letter changes shape with its place in the word, so every note shows the letter alone and at the start, in the middle and at the end of a word; six letters (ا د ذ ر ز و) never join to the letter after them and have two shapes only. Every note gives the letter's name as an Arab says it when spelling a word aloud, with its romanisation in the scheme the level decks use, its sound described in English words, and one everyday word from the A1 deck that shows it, printed with its short vowels and with a speaker beside it. The sounds are approximations, as every learner's alphabet gives them; where English has no near equivalent, as for ح and ع, the card says so. The short vowels themselves are small marks above and below the letters and are not letters of the alphabet, so they are not cards here; the level decks print them on every word.", "author": "", "language": "en", "color": "#9F51B4", "tags": ["arabic", "alphabet", "العربية"], "glossMode": "site", "types": {"ar-abc": {"id": "ar-abc", "name": "Arabic letter", "speechLang": "ar", "fields": ["Letter", "Shapes", "Name", "Roman", "Sound", "Example", "Word"], "cards": [{"name": "Letter → sound", "front": "<div class=\"uc-letter\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">{{Letter}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Name}}\"></span></div>", "back": "{{FrontSide}}{{#Shapes}}{{Shapes}}{{/Shapes}}<hr><div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-pos\">name</div><div class=\"uc-gl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">{{Name}}</span> <span class=\"uc-rom\">{{Roman}}</span></div><div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">sound</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Sound}}</div><div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">as in</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Example}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Word}}\"></span></div></div>"}, {"name": "Sound → letter", "front": "<div class=\"uc-ask\">Which letter is this?</div><div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-pos\">name</div><div class=\"uc-gl\"><span class=\"uc-rom\">{{Roman}}</span></div><div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">sound</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Sound}}</div></div>", "back": "{{FrontSide}}<hr><div class=\"uc-letter\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">{{Letter}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Name}}\"></span></div>{{#Shapes}}{{Shapes}}{{/Shapes}}<div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-pos\">name</div><div class=\"uc-gl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">{{Name}}</span></div><div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">as in</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Example}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Word}}\"></span></div></div>"}], "css": ".card {\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 17px;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n[dir=\"rtl\"] {\n  font-family: \"Noto Naskh Arabic\", \"Geeza Pro\", \"Arabic Typesetting\", \"Traditional Arabic\", \"Amiri\", serif;\n}\n.uc-ask {\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n  font-size: 11px;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  opacity: 0.55;\n}\n.uc-letter {\n  font-size: 76px;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n.uc-say {\n  margin-right: 14px;\n  vertical-align: middle;\n  font-size: 15px;\n}\n/* the four shapes, read right to left as the script is: alone, first, middle, last */\n.uc-shapes {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: 18px;\n  margin-top: 6px;\n}\n.uc-sh {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n.uc-shf {\n  font-size: 34px;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n.uc-shl {\n  font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: 9.5px;\n  letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  opacity: 0.5;\n}\n.uc-field {\n  display: block;\n  width: fit-content;\n  min-width: min(300px, 100%);\n  max-width: 100%;\n  margin: 14px auto 0;\n  padding: 11px 15px;\n  border: 1px solid var(--rule, rgba(0,0,0,0.12));\n  border-radius: 11px;\n  text-align: left;\n  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper-2, #EFEDE6) 58%, var(--card, #FFFFFF));\n}\n.uc-pos {\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n  font-size: 9.5px;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--ink-faint, #6C6A63);\n}\n.uc-gap {\n  margin-top: 10px;\n}\n.uc-gl {\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n.uc-gl [dir=\"rtl\"] {\n  font-size: 22px;\n}\n.uc-rom {\n  font-style: italic;\n  opacity: 0.75;\n}\n.uc-ex {\n  font-size: 24px;\n}\n.uc-exe {\n  margin-left: 8px;\n  opacity: 0.62;\n}\n.uc-gl .uc-say {\n  margin-right: 0;\n  margin-left: 10px;\n}\n"}}, "version": 1, "createdAt": "2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z", "updatedAt": "2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z", "forkedFrom": null}, "cards": [{"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "ا", "Shapes": "<div class=\"uc-shapes\" dir=\"rtl\"><span class=\"uc-sh\"><span class=\"uc-shf\" lang=\"ar\">ا</span><span class=\"uc-shl\" dir=\"ltr\">alone</span></span><span class=\"uc-sh\"><span class=\"uc-shf\" lang=\"ar\">ا</span><span class=\"uc-shl\" dir=\"ltr\">start</span></span><span class=\"uc-sh\"><span class=\"uc-shf\" lang=\"ar\">ـا</span><span class=\"uc-shl\" dir=\"ltr\">middle</span></span><span class=\"uc-sh\"><span class=\"uc-shf\" lang=\"ar\">ـا</span><span class=\"uc-shl\" dir=\"ltr\">end</span></span></div>", "Name": "أَلِف", "Roman": "alif — ā", "Sound": "a long &quot;a&quot; as in father; at the start of a word it carries a hamza or a short vowel; it never joins to the letter after it", "Example": "<span class=\"uc-ex\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بَاب</span><span class=\"uc-exe\">door</span>", "Word": "بَاب"}, "id": "u_arabc_1", "type": "ar-abc"}, {"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "ب", "Shapes": "<div class=\